FrameRelay is a personal-use macOS AppKit host for the UxPlay AirPlay receiver.

The AirPlay engine is derived from UxPlay and is included under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later. The pinned source and all source patches are
kept in third_party/uxplay and patches/.

The application bundles GStreamer, OpenSSL, and libplist runtime components.
Their license texts are included under Resources/LICENSES in the source tree and
inside the distributed application bundle.

FrameRelay v0.1 intentionally disables phone audio with UxPlay's -a option. It
does not request microphone, camera, screen-recording, Apple Events, or App
Sandbox permissions.
